# Ghost's non-secret settings (~/.config/ghost/settings.env; `make env` seeds this file once).
# The desktop app's Settings and its first run write the same lines. Never put a password
# here: passwords go in Ghost's vault (Settings › Passwords, or `ghostd passwords set NAME`).
# Every setting there is, with what it does: .env.example in the repository.

# The model (README.md, "Connect a model"). One provider:
#   anthropic   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in the vault
#   openrouter  OPENROUTER_API_KEY in the vault (or sign in from Settings › Model)
#   openai      OPENAI_API_KEY in the vault
#   ollama      a local Ollama at http://localhost:11434, no key; GHOST_LLM_MODEL names the model
#   lmstudio    a local LM Studio at http://localhost:1234, no key; GHOST_LLM_MODEL names the model
#   custom      GHOST_LLM_BASE_URL and GHOST_LLM_PROTOCOL (anthropic | openai), LLM_API_KEY in the vault
# GHOST_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# GHOST_LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5

# The microphone and speakers: unset, the system's default source and sink, or ghost.mic
# when `make echo-cancel` made it. `pactl list short sources` lists the names.
# GHOST_INPUT_DEVICE=
# GHOST_OUTPUT_DEVICE=
